            <ArticleTitle>Mortality related to coronary angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>858-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angiography is in general regarded as a safe investigation with a low risk of serious complications. Unfortunately, a risk of serious complications exists, especially in patients with left main coronary artery disease or 3-vessel disease. The mortality rate ranges in different studies between 0.10% to 0.25%. The present series, reflecting nine years experience, shows an overall mortality of 0.16%. This figure is influenced by the relatively high mortality rate in the first year of the study. The recent mortality rate of 0.07% has not changed in the last 3 years and almost all deaths occurred in the patients known to be at higher risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
